<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84021" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλώ-ῐμος</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλόϊμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλώω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fit for sailing</i>: </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> of a ship, <i>seaworthy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.29
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				50
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				56.23
			</span></i>, etc.; also, <i>fit for shipbuilding,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ξύλων τὰ -ώτατα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.676a
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of navigation,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤδη πλωϊμωτέρων ὄντων</span> as
				<i>navigation</i> advanced, as circumstances became
				<i>favourable for navigation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.7
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλωΐμων γενομένων</span>
			when the weather was <i>fit for sailing,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				1.63
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν θάλατταν ἐκ Διονυσίων π. εἶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Char.</u>
					3.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς ὥρας ἐστὶ τὰ π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
				</span></i>
			
			
			<i><span class="en">
				5.21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of a river,
				<i>navigable,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥαπτοῖς πλοίοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					7.4.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> of goods,
				<i>sea-borne,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Just.
				<u>Nov.</u>
				163.2
			</span></i>.—Most codd. of <i><span class="en">
				Th.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i> give <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλόϊμος</span> (also found
			in Thphr.l.c.), though in <i><span class="en">
				Th.
			</span></i> they give <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλωΐζω.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
